From f5b3f6f197435feb86e4b91baec5df6808e9edd0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] rpc: serve blockchain and mempool reads from snapshots

Extract this concern so its mechanism can be reviewed and measured independently.
The original split preserved historical source trees. The canonical repair
below changes this boundary and requires fresh behavioral validation.

Original patch rationale (describes the unsplit source, not every extracted part):
Add SnapshotPublisher RCU snapshots for lock-free read RPCs and O(1)
getblocktemplate / submitminedheader.

Original-Commit: 399c3d5cf2aa9602aff967024c7f4053b06d206c
Original-Patch: ecash/014
Split-Concern: read-rpc

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.

Candidate-Repair: Preserve the exact legacy RPC result schema; defer premature
fast-sync status fields to their actual capability owner. Refresh best-header
and IBD metadata on header notifications and header recalculation, including
invalidation and reconsideration. Share the active-chain index and immutable
entry tree; serialize publication with pool writers and never copy concurrently
materialized lazy vectors. Keep central locks out of the RPC read path.

Relocate the original lock-held snapshot-read native fixture and RPC mempool
benchmark to this consumer owner. Existing rpc_blockchain.py first failed exact
schema checks; rpc_invalidateblock.py first reported stale height6 instead of7.
Their assertions remain unchanged and all four wallet-free functional suites
now pass, alongside97selectedBitcoin and123Avalanche native cases. Clean replay
and timing remain separate gates.

Fold reviewed fixes into their purposeful owner without adding repair-only commits.
